    "created_at": "2016-08-28T09:43:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-28T09:43:08Z",
    "body": "I think it will allow page authors to be more flexible around putting up links, as it would make it easier to get page visits. Say when you see a picture with a blue border, I'd be more tempted to click that. Also, we are removing dead code, as I will show in a jiffy.\n\nUsing `a` tag will add more code to your code, that could be unneeded compared to this.\n\n``` html\n<img src=\" \" alt=\" \" link=\" \"/>\n\n<a href=\" \"><img src=\" \" alt=\" \"/></a>\n```\n\nThese two are the same, except we now have an attribute instead of wrapping it in a anchor tag, which I feel and think makes more sense. I don't like seeing wrapped \"components\" like this, when you can avoid wrapping it. \n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
